CORE
reduction_pointer_update.c
--evaluation-order-check
^Evaluation-order reduction: 0 of 3 side effects commute with all side effects they are unordered with$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line 23 y is read before it is written: FAILURE$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
write only writes y when redirect has executed before it. The footprints of
the calls account for all values that q may have, so none of the calls is
considered to commute with the others.
